1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:04,210
Imagine sitting in a room with
somebody else. You say nothing.

2
00:00:04,740 --> 00:00:06,730
You are not even looking at each other.

3
00:00:07,410 --> 00:00:10,440
And yet you know exactly what
the other person is thinking.

4
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:13,180
Not because you can read their face.

5
00:00:13,610 --> 00:00:16,640
Not because you know them
well. You simply know.

6
00:00:17,387 --> 00:00:20,057
A thought passes from
one brain into another.

7
00:00:20,747 --> 00:00:22,497
This is what we call telepathy.

8
00:00:23,331 --> 00:00:26,871
And although people have talked about
it for hundreds of years, nobody

9
00:00:26,951 --> 00:00:31,201
has ever reliably shown that a human
brain can do anything of the kind.

10
00:00:32,024 --> 00:00:34,714
But today we are going to do
something a little different.

11
00:00:35,524 --> 00:00:38,094
We are not going to ask
whether telepathy exists.

12
00:00:39,119 --> 00:00:40,969
We are going to ask something else.

13
00:00:41,819 --> 00:00:45,009
What would have to be different for
telepathy to be biologically possible?

14
00:00:45,937 --> 00:00:49,147
And we may find that stronger
brain signals would not be enough.

15
00:00:49,797 --> 00:00:52,287
Because telepathy would
not be one ability.

16
00:00:52,737 --> 00:00:55,607
It would be an entire
communication system.

17
00:00:58,187 --> 00:01:01,577
Our brain is not electrically
dead. Quite the opposite.

18
00:01:02,547 --> 00:01:04,687
Every second, an enormous
number of electrical

19
00:01:04,767 --> 00:01:07,897
and chemical processes
are running inside it.

20
00:01:08,547 --> 00:01:10,867
Neurons pass information
to each other using

21
00:01:10,947 --> 00:01:14,257
electrical impulses and
chemical messengers.

22
00:01:15,043 --> 00:01:17,163
And because electric currents
create electromagnetic

23
00:01:17,243 --> 00:01:22,013
fields, the brain produces
electromagnetic activity too.

24
00:01:22,733 --> 00:01:24,323
We can even measure it.

25
00:01:25,093 --> 00:01:28,343
Electrodes resting on the scalp
pick up the rhythms of the cortex.

26
00:01:29,402 --> 00:01:31,652
So there is a sensible question here.

27
00:01:32,502 --> 00:01:36,332
Could one brain send information
out, and another brain receive it?

28
00:01:37,009 --> 00:01:39,779
But this is where we run
into a fundamental problem.

29
00:01:40,589 --> 00:01:42,709
The fact that something
is transmitting a signal

30
00:01:42,789 --> 00:01:45,639
does not mean that anybody can receive it.

31
00:01:48,039 --> 00:01:49,909
Picture an ordinary radio.

32
00:01:50,719 --> 00:01:52,869
A transmitter can broadcast
at, say, one hundred megahertz.

33
00:01:54,836 --> 00:01:58,046
But if you put a rock beside
it, the rock will hear no music.

34
00:01:58,856 --> 00:02:01,066
Not because the signal is not there.

35
00:02:01,216 --> 00:02:03,526
Because the rock has no receiver.

36
00:02:04,408 --> 00:02:08,358
And the idea of natural telepathy
has very much the same problem.

37
00:02:09,288 --> 00:02:12,408
Even if we somehow amplified
the electromagnetic signals

38
00:02:12,488 --> 00:02:15,958
of the brain, we would still
need a biological receiver.

39
00:02:16,943 --> 00:02:18,863
Something able to catch the signal.

40
00:02:18,943 --> 00:02:21,273
And then something just as important.

41
00:02:21,563 --> 00:02:24,813
Something able to recognise
what the signal means.

42
00:02:27,403 --> 00:02:30,353
This is perhaps the biggest
problem of the whole idea.

43
00:02:31,263 --> 00:02:34,573
Suppose we could measure a
person's brain activity perfectly.

44
00:02:35,501 --> 00:02:37,151
We see billions of neurons.

45
00:02:37,781 --> 00:02:39,531
We see which regions are active.

46
00:02:40,241 --> 00:02:41,831
We see the electrical signals.

47
00:02:42,812 --> 00:02:45,742
And still none of that tells
us what the person is thinking.

48
00:02:46,112 --> 00:02:49,522
Because a thought is not a
simple electrical signal.

49
00:02:50,313 --> 00:02:52,173
When I think about an apple, there is no

50
00:02:52,253 --> 00:02:54,923
single neuron in my
brain that says, apple.

51
00:02:55,693 --> 00:02:59,593
Individual cells can be surprisingly
picky about what they respond to.

52
00:02:59,673 --> 00:03:02,813
But not one of them
carries the whole thought.

53
00:03:03,618 --> 00:03:06,408
It is an enormous combination
of neural activity.

54
00:03:07,438 --> 00:03:11,668
It is tied to the shape of the apple.
Its colour. Its taste. Its smell.

55
00:03:12,484 --> 00:03:14,694
Memories. Language. Emotions.

56
00:03:14,924 --> 00:03:17,614
And above all, the whole
of my previous life.

57
00:03:18,404 --> 00:03:21,594
And that is exactly why every
brain is a little bit different.

58
00:03:24,384 --> 00:03:27,544
So if evolution wanted to
build telepathy, it would have

59
00:03:27,624 --> 00:03:30,554
to solve something much like
the invention of language.

60
00:03:31,392 --> 00:03:32,922
There would have to be structure.

61
00:03:33,392 --> 00:03:38,282
Not a secret alphabet where one pattern
means danger and another one means food.

62
00:03:39,127 --> 00:03:40,837
Something looser than that.

63
00:03:41,627 --> 00:03:44,567
A pattern that another brain
could learn to recognise.

64
00:03:44,827 --> 00:03:48,797
Because a receiver does not have
to translate symbols one at a time.

65
00:03:49,467 --> 00:03:53,817
Your eye does not turn photons into
some universal code before you can see.

66
00:03:54,607 --> 00:03:58,557
It is simply built, and then
trained, to read whatever arrives.

67
00:03:59,485 --> 00:04:01,715
Which opens a rather nice question.

68
00:04:02,565 --> 00:04:05,495
Would two telepaths have to
learn how to speak to each other?

69
00:04:06,225 --> 00:04:08,815
Or would part of that language
already be there at birth?

70
00:04:09,719 --> 00:04:12,729
With ordinary animal
signals, it is usually both.

71
00:04:13,639 --> 00:04:17,469
A vervet monkey is born already
knowing how its alarm calls sound.

72
00:04:17,839 --> 00:04:20,749
But it has to learn what
each one of them is for.

73
00:04:21,467 --> 00:04:25,517
And step by step, a real language
of the brain could come into being.

74
00:04:26,487 --> 00:04:29,517
And this is where evolution
becomes genuinely interesting.

75
00:04:30,525 --> 00:04:33,535
Because a language does not
have to be built out of sound.

76
00:04:34,025 --> 00:04:38,235
We humans use sound mainly because
we have vocal cords and ears.

77
00:04:39,113 --> 00:04:44,183
Another species could use light.
Ultrasound. Chemicals. Electrical signals.

78
00:04:44,413 --> 00:04:46,843
Or, in principle, electromagnetic signals.

79
00:04:49,573 --> 00:04:52,343
So let us imagine a
completely different creature.

80
00:04:53,233 --> 00:04:56,943
Part of its brain is a structure
that works as a biological antenna.

81
00:04:57,757 --> 00:05:00,017
Something like our ear,
except that instead

82
00:05:00,097 --> 00:05:03,047
of sound it picks up
electromagnetic signals.

83
00:05:03,897 --> 00:05:06,667
And another part of the
brain works as a transmitter.

84
00:05:07,540 --> 00:05:08,990
Suddenly we have a chain.

85
00:05:09,340 --> 00:05:10,790
One brain transmits.

86
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:15,130
The signal crosses the space
between. The other brain receives.

87
00:05:16,173 --> 00:05:17,783
That is no longer magic.

88
00:05:17,933 --> 00:05:20,493
That is a communication system.

89
00:05:20,573 --> 00:05:25,543
And if such a system lasted long enough,
evolution could start improving it.

90
00:05:26,236 --> 00:05:28,946
Better sensitivity. Greater range.

91
00:05:29,216 --> 00:05:32,046
Better filtering of
noise. Faster decoding.

92
00:05:32,636 --> 00:05:35,226
And in the end, perhaps
very complex communication.

93
00:05:38,226 --> 00:05:40,636
But why would any of this
evolve in the first place?

94
00:05:41,366 --> 00:05:43,176
That is an important question.

95
00:05:44,026 --> 00:05:45,416
Evolution has no plan.

96
00:05:46,198 --> 00:05:49,328
It does not build abilities
because they would be interesting.

97
00:05:50,558 --> 00:05:55,068
An ability spreads when it improves the
chances of surviving or reproducing.

98
00:05:55,704 --> 00:05:58,394
And telepathy could be
an enormous advantage.

99
00:05:58,804 --> 00:06:04,174
Picture a group of hunters. No
need to shout. No need to wave.

100
00:06:04,284 --> 00:06:06,114
No need to look at each other at all.

101
00:06:06,814 --> 00:06:09,504
The whole group could
coordinate almost instantly.

102
00:06:10,414 --> 00:06:15,004
Or a parent could warn its young about a
predator, without making a single sound.

103
00:06:15,787 --> 00:06:18,167
Or you could talk in the
dark. Behind an obstacle.

104
00:06:18,247 --> 00:06:19,717
In a dense forest.

105
00:06:20,427 --> 00:06:22,197
The advantages could be huge.

106
00:06:23,010 --> 00:06:26,960
Although the physics would have
something to say about it. Take water.

107
00:06:27,842 --> 00:06:31,652
Sea water conducts electricity,
and it swallows radio waves.

108
00:06:32,242 --> 00:06:34,772
The higher the frequency,
the shorter the reach.

109
00:06:35,620 --> 00:06:39,650
That radio from a moment ago would be
gone within a few centimetres of sea.

110
00:06:40,740 --> 00:06:44,530
Which is why our own submarines
listen on extremely low frequencies,

111
00:06:45,060 --> 00:06:48,290
and why a three-letter message
could take a quarter of an hour.

112
00:06:48,987 --> 00:06:52,077
So a species in the ocean would
not simply have telepathy.

113
00:06:52,887 --> 00:06:57,097
It would have the kind that its
water allowed. Slow. Short. Simple.

114
00:06:58,027 --> 00:07:00,517
The medium would be shaping
the mind that used it.

115
00:07:03,227 --> 00:07:04,697
And then comes the problem.

116
00:07:05,467 --> 00:07:08,137
Picture a city where
everybody has telepathy.

117
00:07:08,827 --> 00:07:10,697
And everybody is using it at once.

118
00:07:11,605 --> 00:07:13,735
It would not be a polite
how are you today.

119
00:07:14,585 --> 00:07:17,615
It would be a million brains
transmitting a million signals.

120
00:07:18,505 --> 00:07:19,855
It would be complete chaos.

121
00:07:20,835 --> 00:07:25,625
So a telepathic brain would need something
we already have ourselves. A filter.

122
00:07:26,542 --> 00:07:29,732
Our own brain does not consciously
take in everything either.

123
00:07:30,382 --> 00:07:35,032
We do not notice every sound. Every
touch. Every smell. Every image.

124
00:07:35,856 --> 00:07:38,366
The brain chooses what
to pay attention to.

125
00:07:39,056 --> 00:07:42,726
There would have to be a mechanism
that says, this thought I want to send.

126
00:07:43,616 --> 00:07:45,906
And at the same time, this one I do not.

127
00:07:46,708 --> 00:07:51,278
And underneath that one sits a second
problem. You think about someone.

128
00:07:52,108 --> 00:07:54,578
But how would your brain know
where to send the thought?

129
00:07:55,469 --> 00:07:57,059
Radio has a frequency.

130
00:07:57,489 --> 00:07:59,319
A telephone has a number.

131
00:07:59,929 --> 00:08:01,419
The internet has an address.

132
00:08:02,329 --> 00:08:05,399
A telepathic mind would need
something of the same kind.

133
00:08:06,217 --> 00:08:09,907
So does every mind carry a
signature of its own? A frequency?

134
00:08:10,937 --> 00:08:12,827
A pattern that nobody else has?

135
00:08:13,611 --> 00:08:16,401
Or would you have to do
something stranger than that,

136
00:08:16,531 --> 00:08:19,261
and somehow tune yourself
to one particular mind?

137
00:08:20,064 --> 00:08:22,014
Nature already does half of this.

138
00:08:22,864 --> 00:08:24,964
The electric pulse of a
knife fish carries its

139
00:08:25,044 --> 00:08:28,534
species, its sex, and quite
probably which fish it is.

140
00:08:29,004 --> 00:08:31,454
An identity, written into the signal.

141
00:08:34,254 --> 00:08:36,584
And here telepathy starts
to get frightening.

142
00:08:37,774 --> 00:08:40,554
Because if evolution built
telepathy, it would probably

143
00:08:40,634 --> 00:08:43,164
have to build something
like telepathic privacy.

144
00:08:44,165 --> 00:08:46,875
Imagine somebody who can
hear all your thoughts.

145
00:08:47,825 --> 00:08:50,255
Not only the ones you
mean to say out loud.

146
00:08:50,962 --> 00:08:55,352
But also whatever crosses your mind
for half a second. Random associations.

147
00:08:55,882 --> 00:08:58,212
Memories. Doubts. Fear. Wishes.

148
00:08:59,165 --> 00:09:01,735
Thoughts that do not mean
that you actually want them.

149
00:09:02,665 --> 00:09:04,765
Suddenly it would matter
enormously to separate

150
00:09:04,845 --> 00:09:07,595
what I am thinking from
what I want to tell you.

151
00:09:08,244 --> 00:09:10,544
And perhaps this is where
one of the most important

152
00:09:10,624 --> 00:09:15,094
abilities of a telepathic brain
would appear. A mental firewall.

153
00:09:18,004 --> 00:09:20,694
And science fiction has
already run this experiment.

154
00:09:20,904 --> 00:09:25,354
Not the experiment of how telepathy
might work. A different one.

155
00:09:25,884 --> 00:09:27,374
What it would do to a society.

156
00:09:28,406 --> 00:09:31,106
In the trilogy Remembrance of
Earth's Past, by the writer

157
00:09:31,186 --> 00:09:35,416
Liu Cixin, there is a species
called the Trisolarans.

158
00:09:36,026 --> 00:09:39,196
They cannot conceal their
thoughts the way that people can.

159
00:09:39,939 --> 00:09:43,449
For them, thinking something and
saying it are not two different acts.

160
00:09:44,359 --> 00:09:46,209
For a human that is almost unimaginable.

161
00:09:47,439 --> 00:09:49,259
We are used to an
enormous gap between what

162
00:09:49,339 --> 00:09:52,629
I think, what I say,
and what I actually do.

163
00:09:53,359 --> 00:09:57,369
Take that gap away, and a great deal of
what we build on top of it goes with it.

164
00:09:57,779 --> 00:09:59,929
Lying. Bluffing. Diplomacy.

165
00:10:00,519 --> 00:10:02,529
Even keeping a secret to be kind.

166
00:10:05,479 --> 00:10:07,429
And now an interesting question.

167
00:10:08,319 --> 00:10:10,259
Suppose we built an implant that reads the

168
00:10:10,339 --> 00:10:13,149
activity of your brain…
turns it into data…

169
00:10:14,004 --> 00:10:17,124
sends that data across
the internet… and a second

170
00:10:17,204 --> 00:10:22,214
implant turns it back into activity
in another brain. Is that telepathy?

171
00:10:23,005 --> 00:10:24,535
Strictly speaking, no.

172
00:10:25,245 --> 00:10:28,015
It is technological
communication between brains.

173
00:10:28,285 --> 00:10:30,435
But for the person using it?

174
00:10:31,005 --> 00:10:32,995
The difference might be almost invisible.

175
00:10:33,965 --> 00:10:37,045
You do not have to speak.
You do not have to type.

176
00:10:37,125 --> 00:10:38,675
You do not have to look at a screen.

177
00:10:39,546 --> 00:10:41,676
You simply think, send me that photograph.

178
00:10:42,566 --> 00:10:44,456
And the other person receives it.

179
00:10:45,126 --> 00:10:47,396
And this may be the more realistic road.

180
00:10:48,186 --> 00:10:51,616
We do not have to wait for evolution
to grow a biological antenna.

181
00:10:52,866 --> 00:10:55,736
Technology could do the same
thing a great deal faster.

182
00:10:56,682 --> 00:10:58,452
The implant can be our antenna.

183
00:10:59,182 --> 00:11:01,052
The computer can be the translator.

184
00:11:01,242 --> 00:11:03,532
The internet can be the channel.

185
00:11:04,356 --> 00:11:08,106
And a second implant can be a
loudspeaker wired straight into a brain.

186
00:11:09,236 --> 00:11:11,776
Suddenly we have something
that, from the point of view

187
00:11:11,856 --> 00:11:15,266
of the user, begins to look
a great deal like telepathy.

188
00:11:15,974 --> 00:11:18,344
But we would not have
to send whole thoughts.

189
00:11:18,994 --> 00:11:20,944
We could send only a piece of one.

190
00:11:21,640 --> 00:11:23,710
And that is exactly how it started.

191
00:11:24,100 --> 00:11:28,470
Because a crude version of this
has already been done. No implants.

192
00:11:28,720 --> 00:11:31,530
Just electrodes and a magnetic coil.

193
00:11:32,342 --> 00:11:36,472
More than ten years ago, a person in
India imagined moving their hands.

194
00:11:37,242 --> 00:11:38,732
Electrodes picked it up.

195
00:11:39,342 --> 00:11:41,312
The signal travelled across the internet.

196
00:11:42,213 --> 00:11:44,473
And in France, a magnetic
pulse at the back of

197
00:11:44,553 --> 00:11:49,203
somebody's head made them see a
flash of light. A flash meant one.

198
00:11:49,813 --> 00:11:51,343
No flash meant zero.

199
00:11:52,126 --> 00:11:54,876
A four-letter word took a
hundred and forty of those.

200
00:11:55,846 --> 00:11:57,756
The receiving brain saw flashes.

201
00:11:58,546 --> 00:12:00,736
It never knew that anything had been said.

202
00:12:01,226 --> 00:12:03,576
The computer put the
word together afterwards.

203
00:12:04,580 --> 00:12:06,280
Since then, three people
have played a shared

204
00:12:06,360 --> 00:12:09,110
game of falling blocks
that way, brain to brain.

205
00:12:09,860 --> 00:12:15,990
One bit each, one turn at a time. It
is slow. It is clumsy. But it is real.

206
00:12:16,819 --> 00:12:20,869
And that is probably the road. A
signal. Then a word. Then an image.

207
00:12:20,959 --> 00:12:25,029
Then a concept. And perhaps,
one day, a whole mental state.

208
00:12:27,713 --> 00:12:29,683
But let us go back to evolution.

209
00:12:30,633 --> 00:12:32,613
Imagine a planet where life has used this

210
00:12:32,693 --> 00:12:35,103
kind of communication
from the very beginning.

211
00:12:35,875 --> 00:12:39,275
Animals with biological transmitters
and biological receivers.

212
00:12:39,355 --> 00:12:42,275
Predators that hunt without a sound.

213
00:12:42,355 --> 00:12:45,145
Prey that can warn the others.

214
00:12:46,002 --> 00:12:48,262
Social groups that can
share what they know.

215
00:12:48,342 --> 00:12:50,992
And slowly, an intelligent species.

216
00:12:52,116 --> 00:12:54,056
Its first word was never spoken.

217
00:12:54,136 --> 00:12:56,286
Because it never needed words.

218
00:12:57,076 --> 00:13:00,046
Its language was not made
of sound. It was mental.

219
00:13:00,898 --> 00:13:04,628
And its culture would have grown in a
completely different direction from ours.

220
00:13:07,508 --> 00:13:09,918
Perhaps there would be no
such thing as a secret.

221
00:13:10,908 --> 00:13:15,298
Imagine a civilisation where sharing
your thoughts is the natural thing to do.

222
00:13:16,012 --> 00:13:17,662
Lying could be far harder.

223
00:13:17,752 --> 00:13:21,042
But a different kind of
manipulation would appear instead.

224
00:13:21,998 --> 00:13:24,958
Because even if you cannot
hide a thought… you may

225
00:13:25,038 --> 00:13:27,728
still be able to shape how
the other one reads it.

226
00:13:28,396 --> 00:13:30,466
So there would be telepathic propaganda.

227
00:13:31,076 --> 00:13:33,876
Telepathic advertising. Telepathic art.

228
00:13:33,956 --> 00:13:35,826
Perhaps even telepathic war.

229
00:13:36,556 --> 00:13:38,866
And of course, a telepathic password.

230
00:13:39,396 --> 00:13:41,736
Because if somebody
can read your mind, you

231
00:13:41,816 --> 00:13:44,506
need a way of deciding
who you actually let in.

232
00:13:47,106 --> 00:13:48,776
So what would we really need?

233
00:13:49,446 --> 00:13:53,856
If we wanted genuine biological telepathy,
we would need at least six things.

234
00:13:54,713 --> 00:13:56,163
First, a transmitter.

235
00:13:56,993 --> 00:13:59,783
The brain would have to make a
signal that carries information.

236
00:14:01,432 --> 00:14:04,902
Second, a receiver. Another
brain would have to catch it.

237
00:14:05,618 --> 00:14:10,148
Third, structure. The signal would have
to be something a brain could learn.

238
00:14:10,943 --> 00:14:12,353
Fourth, a decoder.

239
00:14:13,063 --> 00:14:15,533
The brain would have to
recognise what it was reading.

240
00:14:16,918 --> 00:14:21,088
Fifth, a filter. It would have to
decide what to send and what to keep.

241
00:14:21,891 --> 00:14:23,341
And sixth, an address.

242
00:14:24,111 --> 00:14:26,541
It would have to know which
mind it was talking to.

243
00:14:27,322 --> 00:14:29,872
And that is not a simple
change to one gene.

244
00:14:30,302 --> 00:14:32,752
That is practically a whole new sense.

245
00:14:35,712 --> 00:14:38,752
So if we discovered tomorrow
that human brains transmit

246
00:14:38,832 --> 00:14:42,352
far stronger electromagnetic
signals, that would not

247
00:14:42,432 --> 00:14:45,382
automatically mean that we
had discovered telepathy.

248
00:14:46,070 --> 00:14:48,100
It would only mean that
we have a transmitter.

249
00:14:49,030 --> 00:14:50,420
We would still need a receiver.

250
00:14:51,170 --> 00:14:52,780
We would need structure and decoding.

251
00:14:53,730 --> 00:14:55,340
We would need a way to aim it.

252
00:14:56,049 --> 00:14:59,609
And above all we would need a way to
turn the electrical activity of one

253
00:14:59,689 --> 00:15:04,539
brain into something that another brain
genuinely recognises as a thought.

254
00:15:05,361 --> 00:15:09,331
And that is exactly why the idea
of telepathy is so fascinating.

255
00:15:10,236 --> 00:15:13,406
Because real telepathy would
not be a stronger brain wave.

256
00:15:14,136 --> 00:15:16,506
It would not even be one single ability.

257
00:15:16,996 --> 00:15:18,646
It would be a whole system.

258
00:15:19,552 --> 00:15:22,022
And in the end, a new way
of perceiving the world.

259
00:15:22,812 --> 00:15:26,682
Just as we have sight, hearing, smell
and touch, we would have one more sense.

260
00:15:27,292 --> 00:15:28,492
Another mind.

261
00:15:29,036 --> 00:15:32,426
And perhaps the most interesting
question begins right there.

262
00:15:33,336 --> 00:15:37,726
If we could one day link human brains with
technology, would we still be individuals?

263
00:15:38,756 --> 00:15:42,706
Or would we slowly start turning into
something that we cannot even name today?
